1
00:00:08,250 --> 00:00:09,833
Dear May Deer,

2
00:00:09,833 --> 00:00:11,667
With a lovely family,

3
00:00:11,667 --> 00:00:15,250
Dreaming of growing up each day.

4
00:00:15,250 --> 00:00:17,167
Shy Chuan-Chuan Pangolin,

5
00:00:17,167 --> 00:00:18,667
Quiet, with not a word to say,

6
00:00:18,667 --> 00:00:19,667
Curls up like a popcorn ball.

7
00:00:19,833 --> 00:00:20,083
Curls up like a popcorn ball.

8
00:00:20,583 --> 00:00:21,667
Curls up like a popcorn ball.

9
00:00:21,833 --> 00:00:22,333
Curls up like a popcorn ball.

10
00:00:22,333 --> 00:00:22,917
Don’t be shy!

11
00:00:23,083 --> 00:00:23,917
Don’t be shy!

12
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:24,500
Sing out loud!

13
00:00:24,667 --> 00:00:25,833
Sing out loud!

14
00:00:25,833 --> 00:00:27,417
Let your imagination shine!

15
00:00:30,583 --> 00:00:31,167
Good friends in the forest,

16
00:00:31,167 --> 00:00:33,083
Growing and playing together,

17
00:00:33,083 --> 00:00:34,000
Happy May Deer and Chuan-Chuan!

18
00:00:34,000 --> 00:00:37,500
ODEER MAYO / Happy May Deer and Chuan-Chuan

19
00:00:37,676 --> 00:00:40,082
What’s Lunar New Year?

20
00:00:41,417 --> 00:00:43,417
It’s Lunar New Year’s Eve today.

21
00:00:43,417 --> 00:00:46,167
May and Dad are getting ready to decorate for Lunar New Year.

22
00:00:49,083 --> 00:00:52,083
May, Little Deer, it’s Lunar New Year’s Eve!

23
00:00:52,083 --> 00:00:54,000
Dad, what is Lunar New Year?

24
00:00:54,500 --> 00:00:56,750
Is it like a train going through a tunnel?

25
00:00:57,000 --> 00:00:59,750
Or like getting taller than Little Deer?

26
00:01:01,000 --> 00:01:03,500
Hmm, May. That’s a good question.

27
00:01:03,500 --> 00:01:04,833
Let me think…

28
00:01:05,417 --> 00:01:08,750
Lunar New Year is like the whole family traveling along a timeline together.

29
00:01:09,083 --> 00:01:10,917
But you can’t actually see that line.

30
00:01:12,000 --> 00:01:13,167
A timeline?

31
00:01:14,000 --> 00:01:15,083
Oh…

32
00:01:15,833 --> 00:01:17,000
Then what is “Nian”?

33
00:01:17,417 --> 00:01:19,750
Why do we put up all these red papers?

34
00:01:19,750 --> 00:01:20,583
Nian?

35
00:01:21,250 --> 00:01:23,167
Hmm, another good question.

36
00:01:23,750 --> 00:01:24,500
All right.

37
00:01:24,500 --> 00:01:26,167
Let me tell you how Lunar New Year began.

38
00:01:27,417 --> 00:01:28,417
Do you know

39
00:01:28,500 --> 00:01:29,917
the story of the Nian monster?

40
00:01:30,333 --> 00:01:31,167
Nope.

41
00:01:32,833 --> 00:01:33,917
I’ll tell you.

42
00:01:34,167 --> 00:01:37,583
Legend says that long ago, there was a mythical beast called Nian.

43
00:01:39,083 --> 00:01:40,583
That’s right! Haha!

44
00:01:42,917 --> 00:01:46,667
Every 365 days, it came into the human world at night to cause trouble.

45
00:01:46,917 --> 00:01:50,417
Its eyebrows were like flames, and its eyes were as big as bronze bells.

46
00:01:51,250 --> 00:01:51,583
Its roar shook the heavens!

47
00:01:55,000 --> 00:01:56,500
Roar!

48
00:01:56,667 --> 00:01:57,083
Roar!

49
00:01:57,250 --> 00:01:57,583
Roar!

50
00:01:57,583 --> 00:02:00,667
Dad, there’s no way the Nian monster had a belly that big!

51
00:02:01,667 --> 00:02:05,250
Everyone was terrified of the big-bellied Nian monster and didn’t know what to do.

52
00:02:06,083 --> 00:02:06,750
Then people discovered

53
00:02:07,417 --> 00:02:11,583
that Nian was actually afraid of the color red, sparks, and loud noises.

54
00:02:11,583 --> 00:02:15,000
So they came up with red Lunar New Year couplets and firecrackers to scare it away.

55
00:02:16,250 --> 00:02:19,750
Everywhere was bright red, with firecrackers popping and crackling.

56
00:02:19,917 --> 00:02:21,750
That frightened Nian so much

57
00:02:21,750 --> 00:02:23,333
that it quickly ran away.

58
00:02:23,750 --> 00:02:24,833
Whoosh! Run away!

59
00:02:25,000 --> 00:02:25,917
Whoosh! Run away!

60
00:02:26,833 --> 00:02:29,917
And that’s how Lunar New Year began!

61
00:02:29,917 --> 00:02:31,917
Oh! So that’s what Lunar New Year is about!

62
00:02:32,250 --> 00:02:33,750
Haha! That’s interesting!

63
00:02:34,750 --> 00:02:35,417
Dad!

64
00:02:35,583 --> 00:02:37,500
Why is your Lunar New Year couplet upside down?

65
00:02:38,500 --> 00:02:40,417
Oh, it isn’t upside down.

66
00:02:40,417 --> 00:02:41,250
It’s because Lunar New Year is here.

67
00:02:41,667 --> 00:02:42,917
We hang the Chinese good-fortune character upside down

68
00:02:43,083 --> 00:02:44,417
to show that good fortune has arrived, too!

69
00:02:44,750 --> 00:02:47,333
So Lunar New Year is when we say goodbye to the old year

70
00:02:47,583 --> 00:02:48,667
and welcome the new one.

71
00:02:48,917 --> 00:02:50,333
When you meet people, you say auspicious greetings.

72
00:02:50,583 --> 00:02:52,167
Congratulations! Best wishes!

73
00:02:52,167 --> 00:02:53,750
Oh, I see!

74
00:02:53,750 --> 00:02:55,750
Then I want to help put up the Lunar New Year couplets, too,

75
00:02:55,750 --> 00:02:57,250
and chase Nian away! Haha!

76
00:02:57,250 --> 00:02:59,333
Little Deer, you can be the Nian monster!

77
00:03:02,250 --> 00:03:04,417
May and Little Deer put up Lunar New Year couplets all around the house.

78
00:03:04,667 --> 00:03:05,583
Spring has arrived!

79
00:03:06,083 --> 00:03:07,000
Good fortune has arrived!

80
00:03:10,833 --> 00:03:11,833
May wealth and treasure come your way!

81
00:03:12,000 --> 00:03:13,000
May good luck abound!

82
00:03:13,000 --> 00:03:14,333
May you have abundance year after year!

83
00:03:17,167 --> 00:03:18,417
Spring has come again!

84
00:03:18,417 --> 00:03:19,000
The New Year is here, too!

85
00:03:19,750 --> 00:03:20,583
May wealth come through the door!

86
00:03:21,417 --> 00:03:22,417
Did we scare it away?

87
00:03:24,000 --> 00:03:26,833
Grrr! Grrr!

88
00:03:27,250 --> 00:03:29,917
Hmm. It looks like this Nian monster isn’t afraid of red.

89
00:03:30,000 --> 00:03:31,500
Is that all there is to Lunar New Year?

90
00:03:32,917 --> 00:03:33,167
Ding-dong!

91
00:03:34,583 --> 00:03:36,333
Oh! May!

92
00:03:36,667 --> 00:03:39,167
Wow! Happy Lunar New Year, Grandpa and Grandma!

93
00:03:39,417 --> 00:03:40,833
Happy Lunar New Year!

94
00:03:40,917 --> 00:03:42,917
Hello, Mom and Dad! Happy Lunar New Year!

95
00:03:42,917 --> 00:03:45,167
May, now you can say some auspicious New Year greetings!

96
00:03:45,167 --> 00:03:47,667
Grandpa, Grandma, happy New Year! Wishing you good fortune!

97
00:03:47,667 --> 00:03:50,417
May everything go your way, and may you enjoy good health.

98
00:03:50,417 --> 00:03:52,583
And may great fortune come your way!

99
00:03:52,917 --> 00:03:53,500
Mm-hmm.

100
00:03:54,583 --> 00:03:56,083
May good luck come pouring in!

101
00:03:56,833 --> 00:03:59,833
May, Little Deer, Happy New Year!

102
00:03:59,833 --> 00:04:01,750
Happy Lunar New Year!

103
00:04:01,750 --> 00:04:05,250
Grandpa, Grandma, do you know what Lunar New Year is?

104
00:04:05,250 --> 00:04:06,500
Grrr! Grrr!

105
00:04:07,333 --> 00:04:08,750
Of course we do!

106
00:04:08,750 --> 00:04:10,000
Lunar New Year is all about…

107
00:04:10,000 --> 00:04:11,667
giving out red envelopes!

108
00:04:11,750 --> 00:04:15,500
This lucky money will bring you good fortune in the new year.

109
00:04:15,500 --> 00:04:17,167
Wow! That’s great!

110
00:04:18,000 --> 00:04:20,167
Thank you, Grandpa and Grandma!

111
00:04:21,167 --> 00:04:23,083
Red envelopes! Red envelopes!

112
00:04:23,083 --> 00:04:25,250
Hehe, Little Deer, do you have something to say, too?

113
00:04:26,167 --> 00:04:27,750
Little Deer, say a New Year greeting.

114
00:04:30,083 --> 00:04:32,500
Wishing you prosperity!

115
00:04:35,083 --> 00:04:36,333
Little Deer, well done!

116
00:04:36,500 --> 00:04:37,417
Here, this is for you.

117
00:04:40,917 --> 00:04:42,917
Little Deer, you can’t eat that!

118
00:04:43,583 --> 00:04:45,083
That’s not food!

119
00:04:45,417 --> 00:04:47,250
Good thing I was quick!

120
00:04:47,417 --> 00:04:51,083
Little Deer must be hungry. Come on, it’s time for our Lunar New Year’s Eve dinner!

121
00:04:51,083 --> 00:04:55,833
Mama Deer has prepared a huge Lunar New Year’s Eve feast.

122
00:04:55,833 --> 00:04:58,667
Wow! This is the big New Year’s Eve feast!

123
00:04:58,667 --> 00:04:59,167
Food! Food!

124
00:04:59,167 --> 00:05:02,333
We have hot pot for family togetherness, and dumplings shaped like gold ingots.

125
00:05:02,333 --> 00:05:04,583
Fish for abundance year after year, and rice cakes for rising higher every year.

126
00:05:04,583 --> 00:05:06,583
And long-life mustard greens for a long life.

127
00:05:06,583 --> 00:05:07,417
What a feast!

128
00:05:08,417 --> 00:05:09,833
That’s right.

129
00:05:10,250 --> 00:05:13,417
May, do you understand what Lunar New Year is now?

130
00:05:13,417 --> 00:05:15,667
Lunar New Year is a time for the whole family to reunite.

131
00:05:15,667 --> 00:05:19,083
Even family members who live far away come home to celebrate together.

132
00:05:19,083 --> 00:05:20,583
Everyone together, all reunited.

133
00:05:20,583 --> 00:05:21,250
And of course…

134
00:05:21,250 --> 00:05:22,167
I know! I know!

135
00:05:22,333 --> 00:05:24,250
Lunar New Year is also a time to wish everyone peace and safety,

136
00:05:24,417 --> 00:05:25,917
and enjoy a big feast together!

137
00:05:26,583 --> 00:05:29,167
And it’s the day babies get to bite their red envelopes!

138
00:05:30,083 --> 00:05:33,917
That’s right. May everything go smoothly for everyone in the new year.

139
00:05:33,917 --> 00:05:34,833
Let’s eat!

140
00:05:34,833 --> 00:05:36,750
Yay! Wonderful!
